{title: Come And Dine}
{key: D}
{x_theme: heaven, communion, faith-trust}
{x_source: chrd:come_and_dine.chrd}

{comment: Chorus}
"Come and [A]dine, " the Master calleth, "Come and [D]dine";
You may [G]feast at Jesus' [E7]table all the [A]time;[A7]
He Who [D]fed the multitude, turned the [G]water into [E7]wine,
To the [A]hungry calleth now, "Come and [D]d  - [G]i  - [D]ne."

{comment: Verse 1}
Jesus [D]has a table spread
Where the [G]saints of God are [E7]fed,
He in[A]vites His chosen people, "Come and [D]dine";
With His [D]manna He doth feed
And sup[G]plies our every [E7]need:
Oh, '[A]tis sweet to sup with Jesus all the [D]t  - [G]i  - [D]me!

{comment: Verse 2}
The [D]disciples came to land,
Thus [G]obeying Christ's com[E7]mand,
For the [A]Master called unto them, "Come and [D]dine";
There they [D]found their heart's desire,
Bread and [G]fish upon the [E7]fire;
Thus [A]He satisfies the hungry every [D]t  - [G]i  - [D]me.

{comment: Verse 3}
Soon the [D]Lamb will take His bride
To be [G]ever at His [E7]side,
All the [A]host of heaven will assembled [D]be;
Oh, 'twill [D]be a glorious sight,
All the [G]saints in spotless [E7]white;
And with [A]Jesus they will feast e[D]ter - [G]nal - [D]ly.
